Negative lookup cache for the WasmFS OPFS backend. Every miss in OPFSDirectory::getChild is a blocking
round trip through the OPFS worker and the browser (~260 us in ikvmcraft), where a kernel answers a
repeated ENOENT from its negative dentry cache; JDK_Canonicalize's realpath() retries probe the same
missing name once per path component, which cost ~82k round trips (~14 s) of one Minecraft boot. Each
directory now remembers names the browser reported not found and answers them locally; creates and
moves through WasmFS drop the name. Entries created behind WasmFS's back (JS using the OPFS API
directly, another tab) need wasmfs_opfs_invalidate_negative_cache(), declared in emscripten/wasmfs.h
and exported for JS when the link exports it. wasmfs_opfs_negative_stat() reads the counters.
Applies after emsdk.8.patch (it moves the OPFS_OP_DIR timer below the cache check). Rebuild: embuilder build --force libwasmfs*.

